WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:03.610
Three of three today is another Bernie question.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:10.150
The question is, Hey David, how should Bernie
be handling protesters who interrupt his speeches?

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:16.570
So we actually had a voicemail last week from
a, a an angry Trumpist who said, Bernie is

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.570
weak.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:22.910
Bernie is beta because protesters get up on
the stage and they take over the microphone

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.770
and Bernie just stands there.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:28.369
Now there's a practical question and then
there's an ideological question.

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:35.260
The practical question is that it's lose lose
for Bernie because if Bernie is speaking and

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.590
protesters come on stage and commandeer the
microphone, if Bernie allows them to speak,

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.250
Oh wow.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.720
Bernie is so weak and beta that he can't even
control his own stage.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.740
If protesters come up and Bernie physically
blocks them from getting the microphone or

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:57.130
snatches the microphone away, particularly
if it is, you know, the topless female pro

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:02.690
protestors that have recently shown up at
Bernie's, uh, events, then, Oh my goodness,

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.500
Bernie is a misogynistic.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:10.250
He's physically taking the microphone back
from these protesters and [inaudible].

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.250
So either way he is going to be criticized
by somebody.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.440
Now the reality is go and look at Bernie's
background, right?

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.500
Bernie's background in the 60s sort of hippie
activist movement.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.470
It's all about interrupting speeches, which
is a nonviolent form of activism.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:31.190
So I would not be surprised if when Bernie
has this happened to him, he sees it nostalgically

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.190
in some sense.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:36.670
And it's a throwback to when he was involved
in protest movements in the sixties and seventies

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.909
that did exactly this type of stuff.

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:43.640
Now I also want to point out, and this will
get us to the, to what is coming when it comes

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:49.290
to Bernie's a security situation, there is
a big difference between someone wanting to

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:56.439
speak and be heard versus someone looking
to harm Bernie Sanders or harm another candidate.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:01.490
And if Bernie Sanders is the nominee, there
is going to be no shortage of people who want

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:02.780
to harm Bernie Sanders.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.910
The antisemitism will explode and it's going
to be a mess.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:12.319
So the real answer is if you want to prevent
this stuff from happening in the first place

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:16.269
and never even end up in the position of having
to stand aside while people commandeer the

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:21.599
mic or having to snatch the microphone back
from someone, the answer is you put in place

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:26.269
more security and this is ultimately going
to resolve itself because the major candidates

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:29.590
are going to get secret service protection
very, very soon.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.040
Whoever is the nominee will of course get
secret service protection.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.519
I have a friend of mine who works for a federal
agency who actually is going to be pulled

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:40.829
away to do additional secret service stuff
during the campaign and it's starting pretty

00:02:40.829 --> 00:02:41.829
soon.

00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:48.010
Under no circumstances would the secret service
let anyone interrupt or get close to Bernie

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.010
on stage.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.260
We saw a couple of incidents back when it
was candidate Trump.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:59.480
Remember in late 2015 or I guess it was more
more 2016 yeah, 2016 not 2015 where people

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.340
started to make an attempt to get on the stage
or whatever.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.199
Trump has immediately pulled away the people
that are immediately tackled.

00:03:06.199 --> 00:03:12.400
So the ability for anyone to grab the mic
at a Bernie rally is very soon going to completely,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.620
uh, evaporate because of the secret service
protection that will soon be put in place.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.620
Let me know what you think.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.620
How should Bernie handle it?

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.989
Should he just prevent it altogether with
a stronger security presence?

00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:22.989
Let me know.

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:24.799
I don't think this is the most important thing.

00:03:24.799 --> 00:03:30.709
I do not evaluate candidates on the, of how
they react to people jumping onto the stage

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:31.709
trying to speak.

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:34.099
That's just not how I pick who I'm going to
vote for.

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:36.150
But maybe you're in a different camp.

